<!--**********************************************************************
    *                                                                    *
    *                     AECMA 1000D Change 8                           *
    *                   Document Type Definition                         *
    *                                                                    *
    *                     Release Version 1.8                            *
    *                   Dated 31st January 1999                          *
    *                                                                    *
    * Amendment :-                                                       *
    * 1. Reference new public identifier dates.                          *
    * 2. CPF 99-67UK Harmonize AGE & AVEE variants of the DTD.           *
    *    a. Deletion of entities %AGEDMC; & %AVEEDMC;                    *
    * 3. CPF 98-54UK Restructure to single applicability for both AVEE   *
    *     & AGE                                                          *
    *  a. Removal of entities %AGEAPP; , %AVEEAPP;, %NSN;, & %MANUFCT;   *
    *      due to common applicability                                   *
    * 4. Deletion of entities %AGEAPP; & %AVEEAPP; which controlled      *
    *     applicability configuration . (CPF 98-54UK)                    *
    * 5. Redefinition of entity %NCII; to %NCI; (CPF 98-02UK)            * 
    * 6. Define new entity for Caption Group. (CPF ??-??)                *
    * 7. Define new entity for Product Management Data. (CPF 98-33F)     *
    *                                                                    *
    * Typical invocation :                                               *
    * <!ENTITY % COMPS                                                   *
    *   PUBLIC "-//AECMA//ENTITIES Component Definitions 19990131//EN" > *
    * %COMPS;                                                            *
    ********************************************************************** -->



<!--**********************************************************************
    * Define Entity %AECMA; (AECMA Configuration) containing:- the       *
    * formal public identifier for the AECMA Configuration public text.  *
    ********************************************************************** -->

<!ENTITY % AECMA
  PUBLIC "-//AECMA//ENTITIES AECMA Configuration 19990131//EN" >



